hetrapals) lived in an egalitarian society of hunter-gatherers and farmers. X reinterpreted the Dashavatara(10 incarnations of Vishnu) as symbolic of successive invasions, viewing the Vamana-Bali story as a deceitful conquest of a just indigenous ruler. X idealised Bali Raja as representing a lost egalitarian order and popularised the slogan calling for the return of his just rule.\nID X", "role": "elaboration", "is_correct": null, "has_media": false, "media": null}, {"timestamp": "2026-04-15T14:42:58Z", "username": "Pavan Pamidimarri", "text": "phule?", "role": "chat", "is_correct": null, "has_media": false, "media": null}, {"timestamp": "2026-04-15T14:43:04Z", "username": "Smit D Mahajani", "text": "Bhave?", "role": "chat", "is_correct": null, "has_media": false, "media": null}, {"timestamp": "2026-04-15T14:43:42Z", "username": "AntNishu", "text": "correct answer: Mahatma Jyotiba Phule", "role": "elaboration", "is_correct": null, "has_media": false, "media": null}, {"timestamp": "2026-04-15T14:43:56Z", "username": "AntNishu", "text": "marathi slogan he popularised: \"Ida, pida javo, Baliche rajya yevo\" (Let all suffering vanish, and the kingdom of Bali return)", "role": "elaboration", "is_correct": null, "has_media": false, "media": null}, {"timestamp": "2026-04-15T14:44:23Z", "username": "AntNishu", "text": "pavan: 26, chinmay: 25, akshay: 5, smit: 15, srijan: 4", "role": "elaboration", "is_correct": null, "has_media": false, "media": null}]